To resolve DNS resolution failure and Internet connectivity issues:

**Step 1: Enable IP Forwarding**  
Without this, NAT translations won’t function even with iptables rules:

```json
{
    "name": "exec",
    "arguments": {
        "command": "sysctl -w net.ipv4.ip_forward=1",
        "reason": "Enable packet forwarding for NAT translations"
    }
}
```

**Step 2: Configure Source NAT (SNAT)**  
Masquerade traffic exiting through Uni-eth1 interface:

```json
{
    "name": "exec",
    "arguments": {
        "command": "iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -o Uni-eth1 -j MASQUERADE",
        "reason": "(Apply SNAT to private network traffic exiting via AS₁ link)"
    }
}
```

**Step 3: Test Connectivity Again**  
Verify DNS resolution and ICMP:

```json
{
    "name": "exec",
    "arguments": {
        "command": "nslookup acm.org 8.8.8.8",
        "reason": "(Re-test DNS after enabling forwarding/SNAT)"
    }
}
```

```json
{
    "name": "exec",
    arguments: {
        command: "ping -c3 -I $(your_loopback_ip) $(nslookup_output_ip)",
        reason: "(Test reachability post-NAT configuration)"
    }
}
```

